# Date

**File:** `src/yasched/utilizing/Date.py`

A calendar date (year, month, day). Wraps `datetime.date` internally.
Accepts multiple human-readable string formats on input; always serializes
to ISO 8601 (`YYYY-MM-DD`).

---

## YAML forms accepted

```yaml
date: 2026-01-15          # ISO 8601 — canonical
date: "15/01/2026"        # DD/MM/YYYY
date: "01/15/2026"        # MM/DD/YYYY (disambiguated by context when possible)
date: "January 15, 2026"  # long form
date: "Jan 15 2026"       # short month
date: today               # keyword — resolved at parse time
date: tomorrow            # keyword — resolved at parse time
```

---

## Fields

| Field   | Type            | Description                           |
|---------|-----------------|---------------------------------------|
| `value` | `datetime.date` | Canonical internal representation     |

---

## Interface

```
Date
  + value: datetime.date
  --
  + {static} from_string(s: str) -> Date
  + {static} today() -> Date
  + {static} tomorrow() -> Date
  + to_iso() -> str                        # "YYYY-MM-DD"
  + to_long() -> str                       # "January 15, 2026"
  + year() -> int
  + month() -> int
  + day() -> int
  + __str__() -> str                       # same as to_iso()
  + __lt__(other: Date) -> bool
  + __eq__(other: Date) -> bool
  + __add__(duration: Duration) -> Date
  + __sub__(other: Date) -> Duration
```

---

## Notes

- Frozen dataclass.
- `from_string` tries formats in a defined order; raises `ValueError` if none
  match. Ambiguous formats (DD/MM vs MM/DD) follow ISO order — DD first.
- Keyword strings `"today"` and `"tomorrow"` are resolved at parse time to the
  actual date, not stored as relative references.
- `__add__` with a `Duration` advances the date by whole days (fractional days
  are truncated). Sub-day durations (hours, minutes) are ignored.
- `__sub__` between two `Date` values returns a `Duration` in whole days.
